course: dictionary
lesson: 13895
title: Laden: full of a heavy load
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Laden» means carrying a heavy load, or being full of something. The clue is in the words around it. «The cart was laden with apples» tells you the cart was full of apples and very heavy to pull.
explain: «Laden» can also mean weighed down by a feeling. «He walked home, laden with guilt, after lying to his friend.» Guilt is not a thing you can carry in your hands, so the sentence is telling you that he felt heavy and miserable inside.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «The trees were full of snow» still make sense? Yes, and «The trees were heavy with snow» says it even better. Laden is often used with «with», as in laden with, heavily laden or sugar-laden.
fact: Laden means carrying a heavy load, or full of something.
fact: «The cart was laden with apples.» means the cart was full of apples and heavy.
fact: «The trees were laden with snow.» means the snow was a heavy weight on the branches.
fact: «Sugar-laden» food means food with a lot of sugar in it.
fact: Laden is an old form of the verb lade, which means to load.
exercise: «The cart was laden with apples.» What does laden mean here? | Broken into pieces | Empty and light | Painted in bright colours | *Full of, carrying a heavy load
exercise: «The trees were laden with snow after the storm.» What does this suggest? | The trees were brand new | The snow was melting in the sun | *The snow was a heavy weight on the branches | The trees were very short
exercise: Mum says the cereal is «sugar-laden». What does this mean? | It has no sugar at all | *It has a lot of sugar in it | It is very cold to eat | It is made of sugar cubes only
test: «He walked home, laden with guilt, after lying to his friend.» What does laden with guilt mean? | *Carrying a heavy feeling of guilt | Shouting loudly | Forgetting the lie quickly | Feeling very light and happy
test: Which phrase means carrying something very heavy? | Fast asleep | Wide awake | Lightly dressed | *Heavily laden
exam: Which sentence uses laden to mean weighed down? | The sky was laden with a happy song. | The empty box was laden. | *The hikers were laden with heavy packs. | The shoe was laden with a smile.
